{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128753-mortals-talking-to-spirits","id":1128753,"title":"Mortals talking to spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-14T04:24:47-07:00","id":1128753,"title":"Mortals talking to spirits?","content":"I am running a mortals game, with some elements of Hunter. One of the PCs has the Medium merit (CofD book), and has also taken the Invoke Spirit merit (Hurt Locker). That is a total of 5 merit dots - a pretty big investment. This is a character that is very tuned in to spirits.<br /> <br /> In the group's investigations, he wants to be able to &quot;talk to nearby spirits&quot; (e.g. in a forest) to gain clues. I guess he hopes to use the spirit that has bonded to him (via Invoke Spirit Merit) to act as translator or go-between if necessary. When he asked about this, it was a curve ball for me, because I didn't see spirits as being pervasive enough to do this. I guess I thought that most spirits live beyond the Gauntlet and most of them are dumb Rank 0 beings who can't even really communicate. Maybe I'm wrong? <br /> <br /> Perhaps the player has some experience playing Werewolf (which I have never played), where this kind of request is more normal. <br /> <br /> Before I make a ruling, can anybody comment on how you see this?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12767-spandexandy","name":"SpandexAndy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T04:56:31-07:00","id":1128759,"title":"","content":"There's a spirit for everything except humans, so there's a lot of spirits, and a ton are more than Rank 0. But they are mostly across the Gauntlet, the ones who have crossed are likely looking for people to possess or claim. There's a Conspiracy about this in Spirit Slayers, Les Mysteres, who the player might want to look at, even if you're just running with 'some elements' of the game.<br /> <br /> They tend to be cagey and aren't free about things, though, so if he wants something, he's going to have to do something for the spirit, usually in the vein of something to give it Essence. This can be through something as drastic as human or animal sacrifice or something that otherwise gains attention or importance to the thing the spirit represents, like how the spirit from Invoke Spirit wants the host to keep going through the trauma that kickstarted it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-14-2017, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:08:46-07:00","id":1128852,"title":"","content":"Spirits are common enough that if you produce enough of the right resonance, something will be close enough to sense it and come take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T10:05:28-07:00","id":1128863,"title":"","content":"What your player is doing is valid, though will likely take an Extended Action as per the Open Condition CofD p. 134 as payment if they don't want an angry spirit. If we're talking about gaining Clues CofD p. 78 I'd say Presence + Occult would be appropriate for gaining the attention of a being capable of sharing information. This is high risk behavior even if the Player or Character don't know it. The likelihood of catching the eye of a spirit that'll want to Fetter or Possess the character is inevitable if they repeat this activity. That being said: Urged is a great source of Beats for such a character concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[